= Nova Southeastern University Dr. Kiran C. Patel College of Allopathic Medicine - Prompt 02

#section_label("Prompt metadata")
- Title: Challenges and Helping Others
- Limit: 4000 characters
- Cycle used in this repo: 2025-2026 from Med School Insiders / SDN school-specific thread
- Source: https://medschoolinsiders.com/medical-school-secondary-prompts-database/nova-southeastern-university-dr-kiran-c-patel-college-of-allopathic-medicine-secondary-essay-prompts/
- Local notes file: prompt-02.local.md

#section_label("Prompt text")
If applicable, please describe how your experience with challenges has informed your perspective, decision-making, or approach to helping others. You may include reflections on your educational path, life experiences, or other formative events. If not applicable, please type NA.

#section_label("Shared backbone files")
- typst/shared/challenge.typ
- typst/shared/service.typ

#section_label("challenge backbone")
= Challenge / Adversity Backbone

== Situation
Describe the challenge clearly and briefly.

== Response
- What did you do?
- What tradeoffs or hard decisions did you make?
- Who did you rely on?

== Growth
- What changed in you?
- How will this matter in medicine?
#section_label("service backbone")
= Service / Underserved Backbone

== Community
Name the population or community served with specificity and respect.

== Role
Explain what you actually did, not just what the organization does.

== Learning
- What did the community teach you?
- What structural issues became visible?
- How did this shift your view of medicine?

